  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689602",
      "title": "Event Forwarding",
      "lectureOrder": 57,
      "videoOrder": 49,
      "sourceHash": "308855c20d9b9b3826330c0eb1a83d6e1cda24800c2bd85bc764fba18bf5974e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.14,
          "end": 7.03,
          "en": "For this example, I'm back in the very simple Hello world application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.06,
          "end": 8.29,
          "en": "You find it attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.29,
          "end": 13.78,
          "en": "It's a bare bones project setup, as we've used it multiple times times throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.87,
          "end": 15.52,
          "en": "Get this app svelte file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.52,
          "end": 20.87,
          "en": "We got this main.js file where we can actually delete these props here and then app svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.89,
          "end": 22.57,
          "en": "We can also delete the styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.57,
          "end": 23.98,
          "en": "I'm not really interested in those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.01,
          "end": 25.48,
          "en": "Don't need the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.48,
          "end": 31.51,
          "en": "Instead, now I want to add a new component which can then emit an event to which we can react in the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.51,
          "end": 31.72,
          "en": "app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.72,
          "end": 32.83,
          "en": "Svelte file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.19,
          "end": 40.24,
          "en": "For this, let's pick up the simplified example from the slides we just saw, and let's add a product",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.24,
          "end": 45.04,
          "en": "dot svelte file and let's imagine that would display data about a single product.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.64,
          "end": 48.25,
          "en": "We could have a article for that there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.25,
          "end": 54.25,
          "en": "We might have an H1 tag where we output the product title or whatever you want to name it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.49,
          "end": 59.29,
          "en": "And for that, of course, we need to be able to accept this title because let's assume that this arrives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.29,
          "end": 63.19,
          "en": "from outside, passed down from the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.2,
          "end": 66.62,
          "en": "So here we have the product title defined as a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.62,
          "end": 70.73,
          "en": "And then most importantly, because that is what it's about, here we have a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 72,
          "end": 73.53,
          "en": "Well, we say add to Cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.56,
          "end": 77.82,
          "en": "And now the idea is that we want to emit our own event when this is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.77,
          "end": 86.36,
          "en": "Let's also add a second button where we, for example, can delete the product because let's say we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 86.36,
          "end": 87.44,
          "en": "are the admin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 88.4,
          "end": 89.96000000000001,
          "en": "So we have two buttons here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.96000000000001,
          "end": 91.91,
          "en": "Add to cart and delete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.12,
          "end": 94.4,
          "en": "Get the product title as a prop in app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 94.4,
          "end": 101.69,
          "en": "Svelte, we can now import this product component using pascalcase as you learned it from this product",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 101.69,
          "end": 102.89,
          "en": "dot svelte file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 102.89,
          "end": 105.22999999999999,
          "en": "And then we include product like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.22999999999999,
          "end": 110.12,
          "en": "Now we need to pass product title as a prop here and this can be a book.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 110.12,
          "end": 115.55,
          "en": "And of course you could have an array of products here and use each to output multiple products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 115.55,
          "end": 119.3,
          "en": "But to simply practice this event thing, one product is all we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 120.26,
          "end": 122.57,
          "en": "If you save that, this is what we got.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 122.6,
          "end": 123.77,
          "en": "Got two buttons, we can click them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 123.77,
          "end": 125.3,
          "en": "But of course, nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.72,
          "end": 131.72,
          "en": "Now, for now, just because I want to focus on the event thing, I simply want to throw an alert,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 131.75,
          "end": 134.99,
          "en": "a built in JavaScript alert here in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 134.99,
          "end": 138.38,
          "en": "When we delete or when we add this product to a cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.74,
          "end": 145.46,
          "en": "Now, one technique which I briefly already showed you in the course project module is that you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 145.46,
          "end": 151.43,
          "en": "forward events, you know, that you can register events with the on directive and then colon and then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 151.43,
          "end": 152.24,
          "en": "the event name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 152.24,
          "end": 156.65,
          "en": "And there are a bunch of built in events in the browser in the Dom, like the click event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 156.68,
          "end": 163.13,
          "en": "Normally you then assign an event handler here on the right side of the equal sign between curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 163.73,
          "end": 166.73,
          "en": "And that, as you learn, should always be a pointer at a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 166.73,
          "end": 171.17000000000002,
          "en": "But if you actually omit this, then this event gets forwarded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 171.44,
          "end": 176.75,
          "en": "What this means is that it's not handling this component in this product svelte component, but it's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 176.75,
          "end": 182.1,
          "en": "handled in the app, svelte component and can prove this by adding onClick here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 182.1,
          "end": 182.79,
          "en": "And now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 188.55,
          "en": "Let's add a simple inline handler here where I throw an alert clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 189.46,
          "end": 190.63,
          "en": "Something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 191.17,
          "end": 194.95,
          "en": "If we now save that, we go back and click Add to Cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 194.98,
          "end": 196.8,
          "en": "We see the clicked alert here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 196.81,
          "end": 198.67000000000002,
          "en": "Please note that when I delete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 198.76,
          "end": 201.97,
          "en": "We don't see an alert only on Add to Cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 202.27,
          "end": 208.45,
          "en": "It's also worth noting that you don't see that alert if you remove that forwarding syntax here in the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 208.45,
          "end": 209.62,
          "en": "product svelte file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 209.62,
          "end": 214.84,
          "en": "If you only have buttons without that, then by default events don't get forwarded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 214.87,
          "end": 216.57999999999998,
          "en": "I can click the buttons how much I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 216.61,
          "end": 219.67000000000002,
          "en": "I don't get the alert no matter which button I click.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 219.76,
          "end": 226.32999999999998,
          "en": "Reason for that is simply that the default behavior of svelte is that events don't propagate across",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 226.32999999999998,
          "end": 227.74,
          "en": "component boundaries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 227.74,
          "end": 230.8,
          "en": "So inside of this component I can handle the click.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 231.48,
          "end": 234.96,
          "en": "On a button by adding on, click here on the article.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 235.26,
          "en": "Right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 235.26,
          "end": 236.57999999999998,
          "en": "I can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 236.73,
          "end": 243.84,
          "en": "I can quickly prove that by adding a console log where I say Yo, now you will see that we get this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 243.84,
          "end": 246.9,
          "en": "no matter which button I click because both buttons are in the article.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 246.9,
          "end": 251.55,
          "en": "So normal event propagation works but not across component boundaries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 251.55,
          "end": 258.15,
          "en": "If you want to have your event propagate across these boundaries, then you can use this specific syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 258.15,
          "end": 264.03,
          "en": "where you register the event listener, but you don't define what should happen when the event occurs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 264.03,
          "end": 267.36,
          "en": "so you don't have the equal sign and then the handler on the right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 267.39,
          "end": 271.2,
          "en": "Then this event is forwarded to the next component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 276.96,
          "en": "However, in that component, if we had yet another parent component above that here, if we don't forward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 276.96,
          "end": 279.6,
          "en": "it, then it also won't propagate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 279.6,
          "end": 284.4,
          "en": "So it only propagates one component level if you use this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 284.4,
          "end": 287.1,
          "en": "So this is forwarding of events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 287.1,
          "end": 289.23,
          "en": "But I wanted to talk about custom events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 289.23,
          "end": 290.34000000000003,
          "en": "How does this work?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
